Class fields follow the same rule: initialize in the Constructor, not on
the :DECLARE line (diag.declare_initializer). The Constructor assigning
through Me: is the correct pattern and does not fire.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS TrayQueue;
:DECLARE sQueueName := "default";
:DECLARE nDepth;
:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	Me:nDepth := 0;
	Me:sQueueName := "main";
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS TrayQueue;
:DECLARE sQueueName := "default";
:DECLARE nDepth;
:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	Me:nDepth := 0;
	Me:sQueueName := "main";
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:21-2:23 error declare_initializer: ':DECLARE' accepts only a comma-separated list of variable names - assign the value in a separate statement
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:21-2:23 error declare_initializer: ':DECLARE' accepts only a comma-separated list of variable names - assign the value in a separate statement
